foundation.question_text:
For the polynomial curve graphed below, determine if the degree is odd or even and if the leading coefficient is positive or negative:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-1.5) -- (0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.4:2.4,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.25*(\x*\x-2)*(\x*\x-2)-0.8});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Identify the degree parity and the sign of the leading coefficient for the following polynomial curve:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3) -- (0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.2:2.2,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{-0.2*(\x+2)*\x*(\x-2)});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
Determine whether the leading coefficient is positive or negative and if the degree is even or odd for the polynomial below:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.5) -- (0,1.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.4:2.4,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{-0.25*(\x*\x-2)*(\x*\x-2)+0.8});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Determine the sign of the leading coefficient and the degree parity for the graphed polynomial function:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3) -- (0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.4:2.4,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.4*(\x+1.8)*\x*(\x-1.8)});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
